-- title:
--   Archimedean unipotent fibre integration for GL₂
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, let $K_\infty$ denote its infinite adele ring, and equip $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$ with the Borel $\sigma$-algebra [`AutomorphicForm.glBorelOf`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L57), i.e. the one generated by the topology. Let $\tau_a$ be a measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$, let $n\in\mathbb N$, let $e\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,n\to M_2(K_\infty)$ and let $s\in[0,\infty]$. Regard $K_\infty$ as an $\mathbb R$-algebra by transporting the $\mathbb R$-algebra structure of the mixed space $\mathbb R^{r_1}\times\mathbb C^{r_2}$ along the inverse of `InfiniteAdeleRing.ringEquiv_mixedSpace`, and give $M_2(K_\infty)$ its Borel $\sigma$-algebra. The hypothesis `harch` asserts: $e$ is $\mathbb R$-linearly independent, its range spans $M_2(K_\infty)$ over $\mathbb R$, and the image of $\tau_a$ under the inclusion $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)\subset M_2(K_\infty)$ equals $s$ times the measure obtained from $\sqrt{\bigl|\det\bigl(\mathrm{Tr}_{\mathbb R}\,\mathrm{tr}(e_ie_j)\bigr)_{i,j}\bigr|}$ times the pushforward of Lebesgue measure on $\mathbb R^n$ along $c\mapsto\sum_i c_ie_i$, weighted by the density $X\mapsto \bigl(|N_{K_\infty/\mathbb R}(\det X)|^{2}\bigr)^{-1}$. Write $\lambda=2^{r_2}\cdot\mathrm{vol}$ for the indicated multiple of the volume measure of the mixed space. Let $F\colon M_2(K_\infty)\to[0,\infty]$ be Borel measurable and such that for $\tau_a$-almost every $g$ one has $\int F\bigl(g\cdot\begin{pmatrix}1&y\\0&1\end{pmatrix}\bigr)\,d\lambda(y)=1$, the parameter $y$ running over the mixed space and being carried into $K_\infty$ by the inverse ring equivalence. Let $\Psi\colon (K_\infty^2\text{-side})\ (\mathrm{Fin}\,2\to\text{mixed space})\times\text{mixed space}\to[0,\infty]$ be measurable. Then
--   $$\int F(g)\,\Psi\bigl((g_{i0})_i,\det g\bigr)\,d\tau_a(g)=s\cdot\int\!\!\int_{\{\delta\ \mathrm{unit}\}}\Psi(c,\delta)\,|N_{\mathbb R}(\delta)|^{-2}\,d\lambda(\delta)\,d\lambda^{\otimes 2}(c),$$
--   where the entries of the first column of $g$ and $\det g$ are transported to the mixed space by `InfiniteAdeleRing.ringEquiv_mixedSpace`, and the outer integral is over the product measure $\lambda^{\otimes 2}$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$.
--
--   This is the archimedean factor of Weil's integration formula $\int_G=\int_{G/N}\int_N$ for $G=\mathrm{GL}_2$ and the unipotent radical $N=\{\begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}\}$, in the normalisation where the Haar measure at infinity is prescribed through the Gram determinant of the trace form $(X,Y)\mapsto\mathrm{Tr}_{K_\infty/\mathbb R}\mathrm{tr}(XY)$ on $M_2(K_\infty)$: it converts that normalisation into the explicit invariant measure $|N(\delta)|^{-2}\,d\lambda(\delta)\,d\lambda^{\otimes2}(c)$ on pairs (first column, determinant). It is used in the computation of the archimedean local integral $\int |N(\det)|$-type expressions appearing in the normalisation of automorphic forms on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over the adeles of $K$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_lintegral_mul_apply_col_det_eq_mul_lintegral_setLIntegral_of_map_coe_eq_smul_withDensity_gram_infiniteAdeleRing.lean

